From f88bd92a9c94350677a729dd7bef91485d949282 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 12:53:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00667/11171] [outer-loop] Sudoku harness: add EBT
 (energy-descent decode) + TRM-style refiner
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EBT: bidirectional energy model E(candidate|puzzle), NCE-contrastive training
(gold vs 8 corrupted grids), two decoders — per-cell coordinate argmin + the
load-bearing continuous-relaxation ENERGY DESCENT (Kona's claim: optimize soft
per-cell digit logits to minimize E, givens clamped, then argmax). The argmin-vs-
descent comparison is the artifact-vs-fundamental adjudicator.

Refiner: tiny TRM-recipe recursive refiner (z<-block(x,y,z); y<-head(z); iterate
n_cycles with deep supervision) — non-AR holistic generator.

Both matched-compute (~same params/steps/data as AR). Smoke-tested end-to-end on
the internal 3090 (forward/backward/decode/eval all clean). AR baseline training
in parallel (loss 2.94->0.19 by step 2000).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
